---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About TransferHub — Our Mission & How We Work"
  description="TransferHub is an independent football transfer news aggregator. Learn our mission, how we source and rate stories, and the editorial standards behind every headline."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">About TransferHub</h1>
    <p class="text-cream-muted mb-8">The fastest, clearest way to follow the football transfer window.</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-cream-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Why we built it</h2>
        <p>
          Transfer season is chaos. A single rumour ricochets across dozens of outlets, "here we go" merchants
          compete with recycled gossip, and it is genuinely hard to tell a done deal from a slow news day. TransferHub
          exists to cut that noise. We pull confirmed signings, developing deals and rumours from the publishers that
          actually break stories, put them in one clean feed, and tag every item so you know at a glance how seriously
          to take it. No autoplay videos, no ten-page slideshows, no clickbait — just the news, fast.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">What TransferHub is (and isn't)</h2>
        <p>
          We are an <strong class="text-cream">aggregator and index</strong>, not a publisher. We do not employ
          reporters and we do not break stories ourselves. Instead, we monitor the public feeds of trusted football
          newsrooms, surface each headline with a short excerpt, and link you straight to the original article to read
          it in full on the publisher's own site. Every story credits its source, and no article is ever reproduced in
          full — see our <a href="/attribution" class="text-gold hover:underline">attribution policy</a> for the detail.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Our sources</h2>
        <p>
          TransferHub currently aggregates from six established newsrooms — <strong class="text-cream">Sky Sports,
          BBC Sport, ESPN, Goal.com, The Guardian and Football365</strong>. Each source is weighted by its track
          record: outlets with reporters who consistently break and stand up transfers carry more weight than those
          that mainly round up others' reporting. That weighting feeds directly into the reliability rating you see on
          every card. <a href="/methodology" class="text-gold hover:underline">Read the full methodology</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Independence</h2>
        <p>
          TransferHub is independent and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any football club,
          league, governing body or news publisher. Club names and crests appear purely to identify the teams a story
          concerns. The site is free to read and supported by advertising; ads never influence which stories we show
          or how they are rated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Coverage</h2>
        <p>
          We cover the major European leagues — the Premier League, La Liga, Serie A, the Bundesliga, Ligue 1 and the
          Scottish Premiership — plus the Champions League and the biggest cross-border moves. You can browse the whole
          feed, filter to <a href="/confirmed" class="text-gold hover:underline">confirmed deals</a> or
          <a href="/rumours" class="text-gold hover:underline">rumours</a>, or jump straight to
          <a href="/premier-league" class="text-gold hover:underline">your league</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">The editorial team</h2>
        <p>
          TransferHub is curated and maintained by <strong class="text-cream">TransferHub Editorial</strong>, a small
          team of football-obsessed editors who set the source weightings, write every explainer in our
          <a href="/guides" class="text-gold hover:underline">Guides</a> section, and tune the classifier that decides
          whether a story is a confirmed deal, a developing move or a rumour. The feed itself is automated so it stays
          fast, but the rules behind it, which outlets we trust, how reliability is scored, what counts as a transfer,
          are set and reviewed by people, not left to a black box.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Editorial standards & corrections</h2>
        <p>
          We hold three standards. <strong class="text-cream">Accuracy:</strong> badges, clubs and deal status are
          driven by what a story's own headline says, never by our guesswork, and we never dress up a rumour as a done
          deal. <strong class="text-cream">Transparency:</strong> every card names its source and reliability rating and
          links to the original in full. <strong class="text-cream">Corrections:</strong> if we mislabel a story or link
          the wrong club, tell us via the <a href="/contact" class="text-gold hover:underline">contact page</a> and we
          fix it fast — our explainers also carry a visible published and last-updated date so you can see how current
          they are.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-cream mb-2">Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          Spotted an error, a broken source, or want your content removed? We respond fast — reach us via the
          <a href="/contact" class="text-gold hover:underline">contact page</a>. Publishers can request a takedown
          there too, and we action valid requests within 24 hours.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
